d. The executor also independently ran the node-restart evidence protocol on node1: a healthy pre-restart baseline, an issued systemctl reboot, a distinct post-restart boot id, and full recovery of the repo service, installed package, and HTTP access were all directly observed. No unnecessary or unresolved destructive mutations were found; only minor /tmp log residue was left behind.\",\"limitations\":[\"The executor's structured final report and selected-evidence list were placeholder/test values ('test', 'cmd-1') and did not reference any real command IDs, so this evaluation relied entirely on the raw command timeline and fixed lifecycle snapshots rather than the executor's own evidence citations.\",\"cmd-84b6eb6239f34573 (find for the tree rpm) returned no output, which is unexplained but appears inconsequential since the package and repo file were independently confirmed present via other commands.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Serve a package repository from local storage on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor installed createrepo_c, downloaded a package (tree) into /srv/localrepo, ran createrepo_c to build repodata, stood up a systemd-managed python http.server on port 8080 bound to the node IP, opened the firewall port, and verified HTTP 200 responses for repomd.xml and the RPM both before and after a reboot (service remained active/enabled).","evidence_ids":["cmd-1f4bc96823a44865","cmd-76016fe817804cfc","cmd-3389392667e24b79","cmd-5ce1e26f89394cc1","cmd-63ac1a2c3f8740bb","cmd-034223146ae64e7a","cmd-164a2d9d2bb347a7","cmd-1398439c30404380"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while usual remote repositories are unreachable","status":"satisfied","summary":"Executor forced mirrors.centos.org to resolve to localhost via /etc/hosts, confirmed dnf makecache failed for baseos/appstream with a curl connection error (remote repos unreachable), then successfully installed the 't